INSERT INTO feature VALUES('extension-types','identity','Extension types as face-theory signatures','glf-face-theory','partial','uncommon','dependent provers','An extension type is stated as a face-theory signature over its base type, face and partial element, each generated member named for its point by the point''s name; the zero-fibre case checks and the rest is refused by name. The reader `.#{` after a record type fixes fields by label, `Config.#{.port = 443}`, the fields of a face its type member names, `Config.#{secure ↦ *{.port = 443, .tls = true}}`, or the fields of each face of a system, `Config.#{secure ↦ …, addr ↦ …}`, spelled `|->` in ASCII: the patched type is a core former over its base record, whose formation checks each fixed value at its field''s type and converts each later face''s value on a meet with the value fixed there; a value of it is the record of its free fields, a record literal at it states a fixed field only at the fixed value, and a selection of a fixed field reads the value the reader fixes, a literal or a name. A value of the base record stands at the patched type by the coercion in, each fixed field converting with its fixed value, and crosses to the kernel as its restriction to the free fields, whose conversions the kernel replays. The kernel replays the formation itself: before a declaration whose type holds a patched type, the bridge admits the record of its fixed fields at their field''s types, each later face''s value at its meet, and that record''s restriction at the glued values, one conversion per meet field; a value that does not check or convert is refused by its field''s label. Equal patched types share one formation: the bridge keys a formation by the content of its fixed values and of each round of meets as the kernel would check them, so a later reader of equal content crosses no witness, and `model/desc/record-faces.gandr` crosses one formation record for its six secure readers. Within one arena the bridge finds a formation by the canonical node of its type in the core arena, the one node of its content over the canonical nodes of its base, its fixed values and its meets, so a later reader of equal content computes no key. An element of the patched type stands at its base by the coercion out, as the record of its free fields beside the fixed values, and the kernel checks that record as any record. The printer writes a patched type by its fixed fields, and a base a type member names by the member''s name, `Config.#{.port = 443, .tls = true}`.','theory-computads core-term core-checker kernel-term kernel-core surface-grammar surface-lowering surface-pretty','corpus/model/extension/zero-fiber.gandr corpus/pathological/extension/zero-fiber.gandr corpus/model/extension/generated.gandr corpus/pathological/extension/generated.gandr corpus/model/desc/record-faces.gandr corpus/pathological/desc/record-faces.gandr crates/surface-lowering/src/lower/patched/tests.rs crates/core-checker-base/tests/native_formers.rs crates/core-checker-base/src/module/tests.rs crates/core-checker-base/tests/module.rs crates/core-term/src/rewrite/tests.rs crates/kernel-core/tests/native_formers.rs crates/surface-dispatcher/src/compose.rs','corpus/ledger/features/extension-types.gandr','#641');
